SUMMARY:[ATH] Etegami (絵手紙) Painting: The Art of Joyful Imperfection
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T150000
DTSTAMP:20260904T164637Z
UID:smcl-6a7250e7cca66c2f00a834e5@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Discover Etegami (絵手紙)\, the beloved Japanese folk art o
 f creating and gifting hand-painted postcards. Here\, imperfection isn’t
  just allowed—it’s the goal! Join certified Etegami instructors Amy an
 d Andy for a hands-on\, two-hour introduction to this rich\, liberating wo
 rld of Japanese hand-painted picture-letters.\n\nYou’ll learn to use tra
 ditional sumi ink and gansai watercolors to capture seasonal objects on wa
 shi paper\, pairing bold ink lines and bright colors with simple\, heartfe
 lt messages. Etegami is a restorative\, mindful practice designed for anyo
 ne looking to slow down and enjoy a welcoming creative space.\n\nExperienc
 e a charming side of Japanese art and leave with several finished pieces o
 f unique postcard art ready to brighten someone's day. All skill levels we
 lcome\, especially beginners. Intended for adults and seniors. All materia
 ls provided!\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not desig
 ned for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.
 com/events/6a7250e7cca66c2f00a834e5\nLast synced: 2026-09-04 09:46 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a7250e7cca66c2f00a834e5
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] The Messenger of Peace: Japanese Crane Textile Sculpture
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260927T123000
DTSTAMP:20260904T164637Z
UID:smcl-6a9a6b2760ccaf01c0235248@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join  San Mateo County Libraries and sustainable artist and 
 educator Leila Ghasempor for a hands-on art workshop exploring the beauty
 \, history\, and symbolism of the Japanese crane\; a timeless symbol tradi
 tionally associated with hope\, longevity\, and peace.\n\nParticipants wil
 l learn about the cultural significance of the crane while exploring texti
 le construction\, sculptural form\, and geometric folding techniques to cr
 eate their own three-dimensional fabric crane.\n\nNo sewing experience is 
 required. All materials will be provided. Come and explore art\, culture
 \, and sustainable textile practices. \n\nSpace is limited\, and registra
 tion is required. Registration opens on Sunday\, September 6 at 6:00 PM.\n
 \nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)
 \nRegistration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a
 9a6b2760ccaf01c0235248\nLast synced: 2026-09-04 09:46 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a9a6b2760ccaf01c0235248
END:VEVENT
