SUMMARY:[ATH] Light of the Moon: Mid-Autumn Calligraphy Lantern
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T113000
DTSTAMP:20260904T164637Z
UID:smcl-6a72511788e9bf2800357fdd@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the Mid-Autumn Festival through art and culture! Par
 ticipants will learn basic Chinese calligraphy brush techniques and discov
 er the festival’s traditions. We will explore the customs and symbolism 
 of the Mid-Autumn Festival\, then practice writing auspicious phrases rela
 ted to the moon and reunion. Each participant will create a unique fan-sha
 ped paper lantern\, beautifully decorated with their own brushwork — a p
 erfect piece to take home and enjoy during the festival evening.\n\nRegist
 ration will open October 4 at 10:00 AM.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welc
 ome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource:
  https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a72511788e9bf2800357fdd\nLast sync
 ed: 2026-09-04 09:46 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a72511788e9bf2800357fdd
END:VEVENT
