SUMMARY:[ATH] Financial Wellness Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T193000
DTSTAMP:20260904T164637Z
UID:smcl-6a29f9ab16554cd59fc7e57a@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join the Financial Wellness Book Club hosted by Atherton Libra
 ry and the San Mateo County Commission on the Status of Women. This summer
 \, we’re reading Make Money Move by Lauren Simmons and inviting communit
 y members to reflect on financial wellness\, confidence\, and healthier mo
 ney habits before gathering for a welcoming community conversation on Sept
 ember 10\, 6:00 PM - 7:30 PM. Together\, we hope to build a supportive spa
 ce where everyone feels encouraged to learn\, reflect\, and share perspect
 ives. Please join us!\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, 
 not designed for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibli
 ocommons.com/events/6a29f9ab16554cd59fc7e57a\nLast synced: 2026-09-04 09:4
 6 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a29f9ab16554cd59fc7e57a
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Process and Practice - An Artist Talk with Madhvi Subrahmani
 an
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260915T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260915T163000
DTSTAMP:20260904T164637Z
UID:smcl-6a88b17469166f088b93df6f@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join San Mateo County Libraries\, the Atherton Arts Foundatio
 n\, and Association of Clay and Glass Artists of California for a lectur
 e and slideshow with artist Madhvi Subrahmanian. \n\nDriven by the transi
 tions of her peripatetic life—the opportunities and challenges of consta
 nt relocation—Madhvi explores the shifting relationship between place\, 
 belonging\, memory and identity. Drawing from her daily life and the world
  around her\, she examines the intersection between personal and collectiv
 e memories\, exploring how familiar forms\, patterns and ideas can be rein
 terpreted to take on new meanings and associations.\n\nThe rhythm of repet
 ition is central to Madhvi’s practice. Her installations are often compo
 sed of multiples\, creating immersive and experiential environments throug
 h scale\, density\, light\, shadow and participation. Her practice moves b
 etween sculpture and installation\, creating works that transform space an
 d invite viewers to experience themselves within it.\n\nArtist Bio\n\nBorn
  in Mumbai\, Madhvi Subrahmanian lives between Singapore and Mumbai\, and 
 she has been showing with Chemould Prescott Road\, Mumbai\, since 2004. Sh
 e is a founding member and co-curator of the Indian Ceramics Triennale and
  an elected member of the International Academy of Ceramics\, Geneva. She 
 has also served on the advisory board of Hampi Art Labs\, India.\n\nRegist
 ration is encouraged but not required.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcom
 e to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: h
 ttps://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a88b17469166f088b93df6f\nLast synced
 : 2026-09-04 09:46 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a88b17469166f088b93df6f
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Painting Diwali Diyas
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T130000
DTSTAMP:20260904T164637Z
UID:smcl-6a88bb6a4cb69d003e226826@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Diyas [De-ah] are a form of clay lanterns used across India\, 
 not only to light our religious altars but to light our homes and public s
 paces during Diwali- the Festival of Lights. These lights indicate that go
 od prevails over evil and that a period of peace is coming. Workshop part
 icipants will receive a brief history lesson on what Diwali is\, the story
  behind it\, and how it is celebrated across the Indian diaspora (in India
  and around the world). Afterward\, participants will be guided on differe
 nt ways to paint their Diyas and shown how to light them at home.\n\nDue t
 o high demand\, we ask that community members sign up for a single occurre
 nce of this series so that as many community members can participate in th
 is experience as possible. Registration is required to attend\, and it ope
 ns on Sunday\, October 25 at 10:00am.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome
  to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: ht
 tps://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a88bb6a4cb69d003e226826\nLast synced:
  2026-09-04 09:46 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a88bb6a4cb69d003e226826
END:VEVENT
