BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Computer Basics: Create Stunning Presentations and Documents
  with Gamma
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261007T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261007T130000
DTSTAMP:20260904T164637Z
UID:smcl-6a7f8026be14820029876e67@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to create polished presentations\, documents\, and w
 eb pages in minutes using Gamma AI. This beginner-friendly class demonstra
 tes how AI can help you turn a simple prompt into professional-looking con
 tent\, complete with layouts\, images\, and formatting. You'll also discov
 er how to refine\, edit\, and share your work efficiently.\n\nRegistration
  is encouraged but not required.\n\nIt's helpful to have basic computer sk
 ills\, such as using a web browser and managing files. Participants are en
 couraged to bring their own laptop computer for hands-on exercises. It's h
 elpful if you can create your own account by visiting gamma.app.\n\nAges: 
 Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistr
 ation: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a7f8026be1
 4820029876e67\nLast synced: 2026-09-04 09:46 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a7f8026be14820029876e67
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Sketching with Sami
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261005T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261005T120000
DTSTAMP:20260904T164637Z
UID:smcl-6a481f6edd4fa0c68b5eb39f@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Come join Sami as we sketch the local plants in Holbrook-Palme
 r Park. Together\, we can learn more about what is blooming locally\, so t
 hat when we take walks outside in the future\, we will be able to recogniz
 e what is growing alongside us. Some techniques that will be taught by Sam
 i include how to sketch flowers and how to mix watercolors so that they ap
 pear more natural."\n\nSpace is limited\, and registration is required. Re
 gistrants will be emailed the exact location in Holbrook-Palmer Park.\n\nA
 ges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRe
 gistration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a481f
 6edd4fa0c68b5eb39f\nLast synced: 2026-09-04 09:46 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a481f6edd4fa0c68b5eb39f
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Creatures of Color
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T153000
DTSTAMP:20260904T164637Z
UID:smcl-6a88b9ea69166f088b93e0b2@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the beauty of nature through the bold\, joyful image
 ry of Otomi-inspired folk art. In this adults-only workshop\, we'll draw i
 nspiration from the vibrant animals\, blooming botanicals\, and playful pa
 tterns found in the traditional textiles of the Otomi people from Central 
 Mexico to create colorful animal wall decoration with your own creative tw
 ist. Layer shapes\, experiment with color\, and personalize your piece to 
 craft a whimsical work of art that's uniquely yours - ready to brighten yo
 ur home and spark conversation.\n\nDue to high demand\, we ask that commun
 ity members sign up for a single occurrence of this series so that as many
  community members as possible can participate in this experience. Registr
 ation is required to attend.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag a
 long\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: https://smc
 l.bibliocommons.com/events/6a88b9ea69166f088b93e0b2\nLast synced: 2026-09-
 04 09:46 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a88b9ea69166f088b93e0b2
END:VEVENT
